            "Start is not authorized.",
            "Attempt is not open.",
            "Agent head moved since approval.",
            "Publication was cancelled.",
            "Too many requests.",
            "Internal error.",
            "Service is temporarily unavailable."
          ],
          "description": "Fixed text per code."
        }
      },
      "description": "Closed error envelope of every TVL reactive route (stage, complete, grants, reservations, start, results, cancel, notifications, attempts, deploy finalize and publish-result). `error` and `error_code` are the same closed code; `message` is the fixed text for that code. Nothing of the request is echoed: no key, value, ref, token, name or digest. While the feature flag is off every reactive route answers exactly this envelope with 404 reference_not_found {\"success\":false,\"error\":\"reference_not_found\",\"error_code\":\"reference_not_found\",\"message\":\"Reference not found.\"}, before authentication and body processing, so a disabled feature is indistinguishable from a missing or inaccessible reference. No other code is used for the disabled state. Codes by status: 400 invalid_request; 401 unauthenticated; 403 forbidden; 403 fact_source_not_permitted; 404 reference_not_found; 413 payload_too_large; 409 batch_out_of_order; 409 instant_not_increasing; 409 evaluation_inputs_frozen; 409 instant_sealed; 409 fact_contradicts_record; 409 idempotency_conflict; 409 grant_not_valid; 409 reservation_conflict; 409 reservation_generation_stale; 409 start_refused; 409 attempt_not_open; 409 head_generation_stale; 409 publication_cancelled; 429 rate_limited; 500 internal_error; 503 service_unavailable. Precedence is fixed by each route: authentication and permission first, then body validity, then reference ownership, then record contradictions, then ordering and phase refusals.",
